   "subject": "Differentially methylated: absolute or relative difference?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">When analyzing differentially methylated regions with Methylkit, you need to specify the percent methylation difference, for example larger than 25%  (<span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMono10\">myDiff25p.hyper </span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:CMTT10\">&lt;</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMonoLt10;font-weight:700\">- </span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMonoLt10;font-weight:700;color:rgb(128,0,84)\">get.methylDiff</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMonoLt10;font-weight:700\">(</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMono10\">myDiff</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMonoLt10;font-weight:700\">, </span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMono10;color:rgb(176,64,5)\">difference = </span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMono10\">25</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMonoLt10;font-weight:700\">, </span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMono10;color:rgb(176,64,5)\">qvalue = </span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMono10\">0.01</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMonoLt10;font-weight:700\">, </span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMono10;color:rgb(176,64,5)\">type = </span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMono10;color:rgb(153,153,255)\">&quot;hyper&quot;</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;font-family:LMMonoLt10;font-weight:700\">)</span><div><div title=\"Page 23\"><div><div><div><p><span style=\"font-size:10.000000pt;font-family:&#39;LMMonoLt10&#39;;font-weight:700\"> </span></p>\r\n\t\t\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t\t</div>\r\n\t\t</div><div>Does this mean that the control and test group need to differ at least 25% in absolute methylation, for example 50% against 75% methylation, or does it mean that the methylation values need to differ at least 25% relative against each other, thus 50% and 62,5% ? <div><br></div><div>Thank you for your help.</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
